# 3. Methodology

Testing followed the Penetration Testing Execution Standard (PTES) phases,
with web application testing aligned to the OWASP Web Security Testing Guide
(WSTG) and severities scored using CVSS v3.1.

| Phase | Activity | Coverage |
|---|---|---|
| Intelligence gathering | Attack surface enumeration, DNS and certificate analysis, technology fingerprinting | {{ coverage.assets }} assets identified |
| Vulnerability analysis | Service and version identification, templated checks, configuration review | {{ coverage.commands }} tool invocations |
| Exploitation | Proof-of-concept confirmation, stopping at proof | {{ counts.total }} findings confirmed |
| Reporting | Peer review, adversarial challenge and adjudication of every finding | {{ coverage.rulings }} findings adjudicated |

## 3.1 How findings were validated

Every finding in this report was challenged before inclusion. Each one was
reviewed by a second assessor from a different discipline, then examined by a
reviewer whose specific task was to establish that it was a false positive, an
overstatement or a duplicate. An adjudicator then ruled on the evidence and set
the severity recorded here.

Findings that did not survive that process are not presented as findings. They
remain in the engagement record with the reasoning that rejected them, and are
available to {{ meta.client }} on request. Findings that were plausible but
could not be proven within the rules of engagement appear in section 6,
labelled as unproven.

